# Browsers that support BigInt.
#
# Without this constraint the default target includes Opera Mini and KaiOS 2.5, so Babel
# downlevels `2n ** 256n` — in viem, pulled into the client bundle by @trustvc/trustvc's
# root barrel — into `Math.pow`, which cannot take a BigInt. The page then dies at module
# load with "Cannot convert a BigInt value to a number", before any app code runs.
#
# Those two targets are the ONLY ones this drops (0.04% of users), and neither can execute
# BigInt at all: they were already failing on this page, not working. Nothing that worked
# stops working.
defaults and fully supports bigint
